<BaseLayout
  title="Dengue NS1 Rapid Test vs PCR — Speed vs Sensitivity | Progene Bio"
  description="Dengue NS1 antigen rapid test vs PCR molecular test — timing, sensitivity, cost and when to use each for dengue diagnosis."
  canonical="/comparisons/ns1-vs-pcr/"
>

  <h1>Dengue NS1 Rapid Test vs PCR</h1>

  <div class="card">
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th></th><th>NS1 antigen rapid test</th><th>RT-PCR</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><th>Target</th><td>NS1 viral protein</td><td>Viral RNA (nucleic acid)</td></tr>
        <tr><th>Time</th><td>Minutes</td><td>Hours (lab)</td></tr>
        <tr><th>Sensitivity</th><td>Lower (serotype-dependent)</td><td>Higher (gold standard)</td></tr>
        <tr><th>Instrument</th><td>None</td><td>Thermal cycler</td></tr>
        <tr><th>Cost</th><td>Lower</td><td>Higher</td></tr>
        <tr><th>Use</th><td>POC screening, early triage</td><td>Confirmation, low-viral-load cases</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <p>
    NS1 rapid tests screen fast at the point of care; PCR confirms with the highest sensitivity.
    A negative NS1 during clinical suspicion should be confirmed by PCR. See
    <a href="/products/dengue-ns1/">Dengue NS1</a> and
    <a href="/comparisons/dengue-ns1-vs-igg-igm/">NS1 vs IgM/IgG</a>.
  </p>

</BaseLayout>
